  "objective": "Implement the actual controlled /ask wiring for the narrow LOA/eLA procedural-help query family \"I received a BIR LOA, what should I do?\" by adding a single narrow, feature-flag-gated, fail-open gate in pipeline.js that calls only the pure 09Y scaffold (workflow/controlled-loa-answer-runtime-scaffold.js) and returns a procedural-guidance-only answer for classified-safe queries, while leaving every other /ask query (including all validity/finality/prescription/CTA-strategy/filing-ready/automatic-submission/legal-opinion requests) on the existing, unchanged /ask path.",
  "chosenHookPoint": {
    "file": "pipeline.js",
    "functionInserted": ["isControlledLoaAskGateEnabled", "buildControlledLoaAskEarlyExitResponse", "evaluateControlledLoaAskGate"],
    "callSiteStep": "12.65",
    "reason": "An already-approved, structurally identical narrow safety gate (evaluateClarificationRouteGate, step 12.6) exists in runPipeline() exactly where query/ctx/hook are resolved and before prompt construction/OpenAI generation. It is feature-flag-gated (default OFF), fails open on error, and its early-exit response shape already flows correctly through ask-handler.js to the client with zero changes needed there. The new controlled-LOA gate mirrors this exact structure, runs immediately after the clarification gate's block (so it only applies when clarification does not already claim the query), and calls only the pure, zero-import 09Y scaffold. This requires touching only one runtime file (pipeline.js); ask-handler.js, server.js, and route files are all unmodified."
  },
